
# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

.DS_Store

# Instrumented binaries and profile data from tools/coverage.sh
.coverage-build/

# Python bytecode, anywhere in the tree.
__pycache__/

# Working state written by /coverage-loop: the dispatch queue and the iteration
# log. Machine state for a run in progress, regenerated every time -- committing
# it would conflict on every branch and tell a later reader nothing.
**/.claude/artifacts/

# Scratch notes -- outside reads, drafts, working thinking. Deliberately not
# tracked: docs/ is the knowledge base, and anything worth keeping graduates
# into it as a lesson or a reference document.
notes/

# The beads exports. Derived data, not the store: issues live in the embedded
# Dolt DB under .beads/ and sync over refs/dolt/data on the git remote, which is
# where a fresh clone gets them from. `bd` rewrites these files on every
# mutation -- create, update, close, dep -- so committing them made every branch
# collide with every other branch. 41 of the 42 superproject pull requests
# touched them, and screen-savers#40 was closed unmerged after two full review
# rounds because it could not be brought up to date.
#
# Untracked rather than merged: there is no merge of two exports that is more
# correct than re-exporting from the database.
.beads/issues.jsonl
.beads/interactions.jsonl
